# ripgrep-only ignore rules (does NOT affect git; see .gitignore for that).
#
# Why this file exists: `.gitignore` already lists `.worktrees/`, but ripgrep still
# descends into it, because each `.worktrees/<name>` is its own git worktree and so
# counts as a separate repository root whose parent's ignore rules no longer apply.
# The result was that an unscoped search spent ~90% of its time walking stale
# worktree copies of the same files and returned no extra matches. Measured on this
# repo: `rg -l commentMode` took 12.7s by default and 1.2s with `.worktrees`
# excluded, with an identical 28 hits. At ~13s an agent's search budget is easily
# exceeded, and the resulting partial results cause retry loops.
#
# Keep this list to things that are NEVER a useful search target. Generated files
# that a human or agent may legitimately want to read (site/dist, the built example
# reports) are deliberately NOT listed. To search anything below anyway, pass
# `rg --no-ignore` (or `--no-ignore-vcs` plus an explicit path).

# Parallel worktrees: duplicate copies of the whole tree (see AGENTS.md).
.worktrees/

# Dependency trees and caches.
node_modules/
__pycache__/
.venv/

# Vendored and minified bundles: single-line third-party blobs, never edited here.
*.min.js
*.min.css

# Packaged archives (binary; rg cannot search them usefully anyway).
*.zip

# Test/build scratch output.
test-results/
playwright-report/
.playwright-cli/
audit_out/
